WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.390
- Hi, I'm Rie. Welcome
back to Make it Fancy.

00:00:03.390 --> 00:00:05.550
Let's see what I'm making fancy today.

00:00:05.550 --> 00:00:06.930
- Hi, Rie. It's Janna.

00:00:06.930 --> 00:00:10.110
And I am challenging you
to make Jollibee fancy.

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:12.290
Jollibee was the first
Filipino fast food restaurant

00:00:12.290 --> 00:00:13.590
that I've ever been to.

00:00:13.590 --> 00:00:14.550
And they're killing it.

00:00:14.550 --> 00:00:16.860
I especially love the Chickenjoy.

00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:18.870
I can't wait to see what you come up with

00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:20.703
and good luck, Rie.

00:00:21.690 --> 00:00:22.523
- Jollibee.

00:00:22.523 --> 00:00:24.690
I love Jollibee.

00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:26.940
This is my favorite fast food restaurant.

00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:30.750
Honestly, I don't think
Jollibee needs any improvement

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:32.918
but this is Make It Fancy.

00:00:32.918 --> 00:00:37.918
Chickenjoy comes with fried
chicken, gravy, and white rice.

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:41.250
I was invited to a party.

00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:45.870
My friend brought like hundreds
of Jollibee chicken basket

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:48.930
and that was my first
time to meet Jollibee.

00:00:48.930 --> 00:00:52.169
The skin is crispy and
chicken is so juicy.

00:00:52.169 --> 00:00:54.270
(drumstick crunches)

00:00:54.270 --> 00:00:56.730
It's so good and so tender.

00:00:56.730 --> 00:01:00.780
Just being Asian having
rice with fried chicken

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:02.280
makes sense to me.

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:06.270
Chickenjoy is already a perfect meal

00:01:06.270 --> 00:01:11.270
so I have to make something
very unexpected and surprising.

00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:14.115
I'm excited to Make It Fancy.

00:01:14.115 --> 00:01:16.920
(cheerful music)

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:18.630
All right. Here's what I got.

00:01:18.630 --> 00:01:22.650
Scallions, chives, celery,
king trumpet mushroom,

00:01:22.650 --> 00:01:27.650
Napa cabbage, shallots, ground
pork, ginger, and garlic.

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:31.890
From the pantry I got
peanut oil, canola oil,

00:01:31.890 --> 00:01:36.240
olive oil, sesame oil,
flour, white vinegar, salt,

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:40.950
five-spice powder, Sichuan chili
flakes, Sichuan peppercorn,

00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:45.950
toasted sesame seeds, xanthan
gum, soy sauce, and sake.

00:01:46.110 --> 00:01:48.183
All right, let's get started.

00:01:49.590 --> 00:01:50.693
Make It Fancy.

00:01:51.804 --> 00:01:53.254
First ingredient, Chickenjoy.

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:55.830
Keep some little surgery.

00:01:55.830 --> 00:02:00.180
Separate chicken skin. Easily comes off.

00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:02.910
Separate meat from the bone.

00:02:02.910 --> 00:02:06.210
I like thigh better
flavor-wise but I feel like

00:02:06.210 --> 00:02:09.780
if you order breast, comes with more food.

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:10.800
It's life hack.

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:13.800
Put chicken bone, one shallot,

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:17.760
one stalk celery, and ginger slices.

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:22.020
Three cloves of garlic, two cups of water

00:02:22.020 --> 00:02:23.880
into pressure cooker.

00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:25.230
One pinch of salt.

00:02:25.230 --> 00:02:27.363
Cook this for 60 minutes.

00:02:32.106 --> 00:02:33.330
(metal clanging)

00:02:33.330 --> 00:02:34.773
Wait, how does this work?

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:41.670
60 minutes later my stock is ready.

00:02:41.670 --> 00:02:45.000
Smells good. And I'm going to strain.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:46.413
Now I wanna taste it.

00:02:47.730 --> 00:02:49.680
Needs much more salt.

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:51.570
I made a delicious Jollibee broth

00:02:51.570 --> 00:02:54.570
and I'm gonna set it aside
and move on the next step.

00:02:54.570 --> 00:02:56.010
Two cups of oil.

00:02:56.010 --> 00:02:59.954
One minced shallot, five
cloves of minced garlic,

00:02:59.954 --> 00:03:03.390
two tablespoon of Sichuan peppercorn.

00:03:03.390 --> 00:03:05.584
For those who never
had Sichuan peppercorn,

00:03:05.584 --> 00:03:09.450
it kind of tingles your tongue and lips.

00:03:09.450 --> 00:03:12.870
It's really fun flavor and sensation.

00:03:12.870 --> 00:03:15.480
Cook this in low and slow.

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:20.480
About 15 minutes until the
temperature goes 215 degree

00:03:20.617 --> 00:03:25.410
and shallot is a little bit
crisped up, but not too brown.

00:03:25.410 --> 00:03:28.110
It has been cooking about 15 minutes

00:03:28.110 --> 00:03:31.634
and I'm going to use the
skin I removed earlier.

00:03:31.634 --> 00:03:34.763
Chop kind of same size as the shallot.

00:03:34.763 --> 00:03:39.060
I made a video about bees for Tasty.

00:03:39.060 --> 00:03:43.320
I went to somebody's backyard
and he was making honey.

00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:46.350
So I know one or two things about bees.

00:03:46.350 --> 00:03:49.470
- [Producer] Jollibee, the
mascot, has a girlfriend.

00:03:49.470 --> 00:03:50.947
- Is she butterfly?

00:03:50.947 --> 00:03:51.780
[Producer] - She's not an insect.

00:03:51.780 --> 00:03:54.597
(both laughs)

00:03:54.597 --> 00:03:56.970
- [Rie] Add this into the oil.

00:03:56.970 --> 00:04:00.630
Cook another 15 minutes until
shallot is crispy and golden.

00:04:00.630 --> 00:04:03.186
I have Sichuan pepper,

00:04:03.186 --> 00:04:05.610
three fourth cup of chili flake,

00:04:05.610 --> 00:04:09.473
one and half teaspoon
of five spice powder,

00:04:09.473 --> 00:04:12.120
one teaspoon of salt.

00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:14.010
And I'm going to pour over.

00:04:14.010 --> 00:04:17.640
Mix well. Let it sit at least 30 minutes.

00:04:17.640 --> 00:04:21.027
I'm going to use all rice
came in the Chickenjoy box.

00:04:21.027 --> 00:04:23.970
Add two tablespoon of water.

00:04:23.970 --> 00:04:27.300
Pulse until like a paste texture.

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:31.231
Scrape on the side, and I'm
going to add water as needed.

00:04:31.231 --> 00:04:33.000
(blender roars)

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:34.170
Add in the bowl.

00:04:34.170 --> 00:04:38.160
This looks good, but this
still needs more ingredients.

00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:40.947
I have 120 gram of flour.

00:04:40.947 --> 00:04:44.751
Add 60 gram of the rice paste I made.

00:04:44.751 --> 00:04:47.970
Three full teaspoon of xanthan gum,

00:04:47.970 --> 00:04:50.430
and the xanthan gum is kind of additive.

00:04:50.430 --> 00:04:53.070
It helps hold the shape together.

00:04:53.070 --> 00:04:57.612
Four tablespoon of water,
two teaspoon of olive oil.

00:04:57.612 --> 00:05:00.540
Mix everything together.

00:05:00.540 --> 00:05:02.520
And once it started coming together,

00:05:02.520 --> 00:05:04.350
I'm going to knead by hand.

00:05:04.350 --> 00:05:06.750
Use a little bench flour.

00:05:06.750 --> 00:05:10.110
Jollibee rice dough is a little bit rough

00:05:10.110 --> 00:05:12.902
because, you know, even we
process in food processor there,

00:05:12.902 --> 00:05:15.540
it's like a little bit grain rice.

00:05:15.540 --> 00:05:18.000
I think it's still pretty good.

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:21.420
Taste would be nice 'cause
rice is a little sweet,

00:05:21.420 --> 00:05:22.253
but we will see.

00:05:22.253 --> 00:05:25.281
So I'm going to knead until the dough

00:05:25.281 --> 00:05:28.682
is a little bit smoother on the surface.

00:05:28.682 --> 00:05:32.030
I think this is good,
almost like a pasta dough.

00:05:32.030 --> 00:05:35.820
It is a little bit smooth and bouncy.

00:05:35.820 --> 00:05:38.460
Put it in the bowl, cover it with plastic,

00:05:38.460 --> 00:05:40.170
and rest for 30 minutes.

00:05:40.170 --> 00:05:42.060
So I have fried chicken meat.

00:05:42.060 --> 00:05:43.620
I'm going to mince.

00:05:43.620 --> 00:05:46.320
- [Producer] Rie, when do
you think Jollibee came out?

00:05:47.793 --> 00:05:48.626
- 1987.

00:05:49.540 --> 00:05:50.758
- [Producer] 1978.

00:05:50.758 --> 00:05:53.220
- [Rie] Put chicken in the bowl.

00:05:53.220 --> 00:05:55.567
Half pound of ground pork,

00:05:55.567 --> 00:05:58.860
one cup of chopped Napa cabbage,

00:05:58.860 --> 00:06:02.130
half cup of king trumpet mushroom,

00:06:02.130 --> 00:06:03.789
quarter cup of chives,

00:06:03.789 --> 00:06:06.810
two tablespoon gravy,

00:06:06.810 --> 00:06:09.480
one tablespoon of soy sauce,

00:06:09.480 --> 00:06:12.450
half tablespoon of sesame oil.

00:06:12.450 --> 00:06:17.450
Grate two cloves of garlic,
grate half teaspoon of ginger.

00:06:19.110 --> 00:06:21.390
One tablespoon of sake.

00:06:21.390 --> 00:06:24.270
Mix everything with using my hand.

00:06:24.270 --> 00:06:27.630
Just make sure everything combines well.

00:06:27.630 --> 00:06:31.170
I think filling is ready
but I have more stuff to do.

00:06:31.170 --> 00:06:34.530
I have the dough I've been resting.

00:06:34.530 --> 00:06:37.800
Sprinkle some flour on the surface.

00:06:37.800 --> 00:06:41.400
Roll this out into one long log.

00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:43.200
I'm going to cut this.

00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:46.800
I'm cutting them into pieces.

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:50.610
Roll it out into circular.

00:06:50.610 --> 00:06:54.450
You have to do it from
the side 'cause the center

00:06:54.450 --> 00:06:57.150
should be a little bit
thicker than the edge,

00:06:57.150 --> 00:06:58.560
'cause you are folding in.

00:06:58.560 --> 00:07:02.790
I think dough is actually
working pretty good.

00:07:02.790 --> 00:07:05.996
Cover with plastic while
I'm working on other dough

00:07:05.996 --> 00:07:08.880
so it doesn't dry out.

00:07:08.880 --> 00:07:12.705
You want to make about
four to five inches circle.

00:07:12.705 --> 00:07:14.737
It's not like making cookie.

00:07:14.737 --> 00:07:17.190
If you rolling at once,

00:07:17.190 --> 00:07:20.070
outside is getting a little bit thicker.

00:07:20.070 --> 00:07:23.610
So you want to make it outside
it's thinner than the center.

00:07:23.610 --> 00:07:25.379
All right, it's time to get fancy.

00:07:25.379 --> 00:07:28.879
(enchanting violin music)

00:07:38.340 --> 00:07:40.020
I made dumplings.

00:07:40.020 --> 00:07:42.180
Let's fry them up.

00:07:42.180 --> 00:07:44.310
One tablespoon of oil.

00:07:44.310 --> 00:07:46.403
Put this in the pan.

00:07:46.403 --> 00:07:48.840
Heat up the pan over medium-high heat.

00:07:48.840 --> 00:07:52.920
Sear the dumpling until
it has a nice brown color

00:07:52.920 --> 00:07:53.970
on the bottom.

00:07:53.970 --> 00:07:57.900
Cook them in batches because
I don't want to crowd the pan.

00:07:57.900 --> 00:08:00.267
After you get nice brown
color on the bottom,

00:08:00.267 --> 00:08:03.780
add three tablespoon of Jollibee broth,

00:08:03.780 --> 00:08:06.390
and cook dumpling about five minutes

00:08:06.390 --> 00:08:08.850
or until inside it's completely cooked.

00:08:08.850 --> 00:08:11.760
All the chicken stock is evaporated.

00:08:11.760 --> 00:08:13.576
Dough it looks a little bit bake.

00:08:13.576 --> 00:08:15.180
And I think it's ready.

00:08:15.180 --> 00:08:18.870
Transfer to the tray and
I'm going to cook the rest.

00:08:18.870 --> 00:08:20.370
I made a dumpling filling

00:08:20.370 --> 00:08:25.290
with Jollibee fried
chicken's meat and gravy.

00:08:25.290 --> 00:08:29.250
I made dumpling wrapper
using Jollibee's rice.

00:08:29.250 --> 00:08:33.030
Chili oil using Jollibee
fried chicken crispy skin.

00:08:33.030 --> 00:08:35.486
Let's plate. Nice and crispy.

00:08:35.486 --> 00:08:40.486
Pour chili oil and some
sesame seeds garnish.

00:08:40.530 --> 00:08:42.616
And, we are done.

00:08:42.616 --> 00:08:45.699
(slow melodic music)

00:08:52.951 --> 00:08:56.057
Jollibee dumpling with
chili oil. Very fancy.

00:08:56.057 --> 00:08:59.340
(upbeat music)

00:08:59.340 --> 00:09:02.054
Welcome Janna, to Make It Fancy.

00:09:02.054 --> 00:09:03.191
- Thank you. Oh my God.

00:09:03.191 --> 00:09:04.590
This is like dream being on here.

00:09:04.590 --> 00:09:05.790
(Rie cheers)

00:09:05.790 --> 00:09:10.740
- So I'm so happy you challenged
me and I made dumpling.

00:09:10.740 --> 00:09:11.972
- Is this real?

00:09:11.972 --> 00:09:14.340
I mean not surprised that
you would make this fancy

00:09:14.340 --> 00:09:15.720
but I did not expect dumplings.

00:09:15.720 --> 00:09:16.553
- [Both] Cheers.

00:09:18.490 --> 00:09:19.323
- [Rie] Mm.

00:09:19.323 --> 00:09:20.430
- [Janna] Mm.

00:09:20.430 --> 00:09:21.263
This is Jollibee?

00:09:21.263 --> 00:09:22.096
- Mhm.

00:09:23.370 --> 00:09:25.980
- I didn't know Jollibee
could be this fancy.

00:09:25.980 --> 00:09:28.887
Filipinos are the firm believer
of the Jollibee supremacy.

00:09:28.887 --> 00:09:31.397
It's so cool that you
were able to take Jollibee

00:09:31.397 --> 00:09:33.720
and make it into something
completely different,

00:09:33.720 --> 00:09:34.770
and new and exciting.

00:09:34.770 --> 00:09:37.590
It's like a perfect like
fusion of two cultures.

00:09:37.590 --> 00:09:39.810
Maybe Jollibee could take some notes.

00:09:39.810 --> 00:09:43.599
- So, Janna did I make
Jollibee Chickenjoy fancy?

00:09:43.599 --> 00:09:45.540
- A thousand percent fancy.

00:09:45.540 --> 00:09:46.490
- Thousand percent.

00:09:47.360 --> 00:09:50.050
- By the way, I love
this Make It Fancy merch.

00:09:50.050 --> 00:09:52.107
- Thank you. You can get it.

00:09:52.107 --> 00:09:54.420
ShopMakeItFancy.com

00:09:54.420 --> 00:09:56.274
- Oh, there's even a website. Okay.

00:09:56.274 --> 00:09:58.570
- All right. We have
one last things to do.

00:09:58.570 --> 00:09:59.700
- It's the dance?

00:09:59.700 --> 00:10:00.533
- Yes.

00:10:00.533 --> 00:10:01.366
3, 2, 1.

00:10:01.366 --> 00:10:02.417
- [Both] Make It Fancy.

00:10:02.417 --> 00:10:03.425
- I went the other way.

00:10:03.425 --> 00:10:05.342
- [Both] Make It Fancy.

00:10:06.876 --> 00:10:09.876
- (soft Jazz music)

